WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:08.960
The year 2006 marks the second centenary
since the invention of the cocktail.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:36.130
May I ask, do you enjoy a tipple?

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.140
Maybe a glass of beer after a hot bath?

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.760
One poured into a cold glass, with
a good head and downed in one.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:49.100
We each have our preference
when it comes to enjoying a libation.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.940
A chat with an old pal, or whispering
sweet nothings into a lover's ear.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.030
Or perhaps while deep in thought with
the glass ever so slightly tilted.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.370
This bar welcomes guests of
all types through its doors.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.700
Every drink has a story.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.540
And every story has a drink
to accompany it.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.670
This is the story of a Iittle bar
in a secluded corner of Ginza.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.380
The bar, Eden hall,
and its curious beginnings.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:26.930
So pull up a pew, and come enjoy
a "Glass of the Gods" in our company.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.150
The Suze Champagne cocktail, "Etude".

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:44.490
I Iiked it so much that I drank it
all the time, when I Iived in France.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:52.330
One sip of this drink and the day's
stresses would wash away in an instant.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.170
Found in the backstreets of Ginza,

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.800
no one could blame you for missing it.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.060
I did pause a moment
before stepping through the door.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:08.520
But I'm very glad I did,
as it helped me relax,

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:13.100
sweeping away any worries
I had about work the next day.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.230
Which cocktail should I try next,
I wonder.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.120
A Suze Gimlet.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:27.580
Is this...?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.120
Or would you have preferred
a Charles Jordan?

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.790
Or another liqueur entirely?

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.500
Oh, no. This is fine.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:41.380
Etude? Suze Gimlet? Charles Jordan?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.220
Those are the cocktails I ordered
while I was in France...

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.180
He even knows the order
in which I drank them...

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:57.860
That's right! I think I ordered a drink
from him in a bar in a Faris hotel.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:02.030
I can't believe he remembers
my order from that one time.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.110
I suddenly feel so happy.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:07.870
This is how I met...

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.750
the bartender known as
the "Glass of the Gods".

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.920
Ryu Sasakura.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:25.760
You're kidding, right?
That's no more than bartender hokum.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:30.260
Who could remember the order someone
got their drinks in just hearing it once?

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.270
And years ago at that! You're dreaming.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:39.270
It's true... Everything back then
was just a bit of a joke to me.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.110
The reason for that was...

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:47.200
Let me tell you right now. I have zero
expectations from you barmen.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.370
In light of the full remodelling
this hotel will be undergoing,

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:54.910
I plan on turning this into a bar which
understands its customers' needs.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.420
Bars that rely on the barman's
experience or skill are out!

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.300
A famous interior designer
might be able to bring in clients,

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.130
but no one gives a damn if you're
a well-known barman.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:09.600
Nonetheless, we need you to have
a certain level of ability.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.890
Which is why I want you to make me
your best cocktail,

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:16.480
and if you satisfy the repuirements,
I will Iet you run this bar.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:17.730
Got it?

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:24.690
As you can see,
this man apparently hates bartenders.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.820
He calls them "barmen".

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.660
And treats them Iike simple tools
for his bar project.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.540
I do wonder what kind of bar
this will turn into.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:40.210
I'm sure it will be one that takes
the shape of Mr Kamishima's heart.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.420
A bar that I'm sure to hate...

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.340
You're all ready then?
You can go first.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:50.140
Yes, sir.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.390
I will make you a Martini.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.400
Please, enjoy.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:15.290
Have I finished eating?
Or am I about to dine?

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.290
You didn't say either way...

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.210
The Martini is a strong cocktail.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:26.960
What an idea making something Iike that
for me without knowing if I'm full or not.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.420
Next!

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.430
I will make you Grasshopper.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.140
In that case...

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.310
I'll take it "pousse-café" style.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:36.060
Yes, sir...

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.100
Pousse-café style.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:45.440
A style of layering the ingredients of
differing densities without them mixing.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:46.690
But...

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.910
They all got mixed...

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:56.580
I wasn't expecting the sudden change.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:00.080
Is that disdain towards
the customer I'm detecting?

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.580
You're the disdainful one!

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.840
The lady's right. I admit it.
I felt disdain towards them.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:12.090
As evidenced by the fact that I absolutely
refused to call them "bartenders",

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:15.510
but "barmen",
uttered in a deprecating tone.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:28.280
This is neither bad nor good.
It's just about what I'd expect...

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:34.370
I suppose you could say I was
puite obstinate back then.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:38.910
Reason being that I could not stand bars.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:43.420
Pretentious barmen and doors so heavy
you'd think they wanted to keep you out!

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:48.460
I couldn't understand
their allure in the slightest.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.970
But then...

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:56.800
I, of all people, got assigned
with remodelling a hotel bar...

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:01.270
Of course I had no complaints,
this was my job after all.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:02.980
"I would be delighted." I replied.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.520
What are you doing?
We're already well behind schedule!

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.820
Did you get the marketing wrong?
Do it over!

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.650
Where are the prospective barmen?

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.070
Throw money at them if you have to!
Bring me some decent staff!

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:18.780
Same goes for the booze.
Bring me anything!

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.830
Just make sure the back is full of
luxurious looking liquor!

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:27.710
Quit dragging your feet and
get the bar design finished!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.550
I knew I'd hate this kind of bar!

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.050
Shut it! I don't want to hear it!

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.300
We're having a meeting tonight.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.640
I don't care if you pull an all-nighter.
I want results not excuses!

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.440
It looks more like some ruins
than a pre-modelling.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:52.110
Actually, this run-down atmosphere
might be kind of original...

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.900
Are you nuts?

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.950
What were you thinking?

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.410
This latest project of yours
is going to pot!

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.580
Your subordinates are complaining, too.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.920
Listen here. Get at least the design
for this thing finished pronto!

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.920
Make it a bar people will want to
break down the door to get into!

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:24.020
Who gives a rat's ass what the place
looks like as long as it has booze!

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:27.520
I don't need to get rowdy
in some izakaya...

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.980
Give me an old street stall
any day of the week!

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.480
Or even a nice cold beer after
getting out of the bath...

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:35.110
WATER

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.660
At any rate, I absolutely loathe bars!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.510
What's this...?

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.730
The reflection of a lone door in a puddle.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:13.020
This was the curious beginnings of
Mr Kamishima's encounter with Eden hall.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.620
When I Iook back on it now, it really was
a very curious encounter.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.210
That someone like myself,
who hated bars,

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:32.840
was staring at Eden hall as though
something was drawing me in.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.550
And then...

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.550
Welcome.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.560
What is this object, young man?

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.480
It is an ice sculpture in the form of
the Eden hall glass.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:56.820
Eden hall?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:00.820
Yes.
There is a legend in the north of England.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:04.910
It is said that one evening,
some fairies were holding a banquet.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.240
They were surprised so see a human arrive.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.200
And so they all scattered immediately.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.960
In that instant, a single glass
was left behind, and on it was inscribed,

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:20.010
"Should this glass be broken, the joy
of Eden hall will be lost forever."

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:26.220
Since that day, we safeguarded the form
of "Eden hall's fortune" as it is known,

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.850
through its representation in ice,
and by naming this bar after it.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.060
A legend that tells of a glass
that must not be broken...

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.570
This wouldn't be the barman
they call the "Glass of the Gods"...?

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:38.980
Surely he's too young.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.570
Did you find us through an introduction?

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.110
Introduction?

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.580
I need an introduction to come here, do I?

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.740
No, not at all.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.330
Please accept my apologies,
if I offended you.

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:56.790
You say that, but are you sure you
don't pick and choose customers?

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.670
That door's so heavy one might think
you're trying to keep customers out.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:03.930
A bar is a hideout after all.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.550
A hideout?

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:09.770
That's right. A place where gangs
can lay low for a while.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:13.560
Because it's a place to hide,
the door needs to be weighty.

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:17.440
And the name plate is small
so as to go unnoticed by passers-by.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:22.990
But once you've set foot inside,
you can forget the world out there.

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.820
You can forget your
position in life and age,

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:27.950
and come face-to-face
with your true self.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:31.660
All thanks to that heavy door.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.000
If you say so, kid...

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:39.340
And by any chance are you the bartender
that can remember orders from years back?

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.590
Indeed, that is one of my specialities,

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.390
but that is also simply
part of being a bartender...

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:48.350
"Bartender" my ass.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.930
All you lot do is make and
serve drinks following a recipe.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.140
Must be nice making money
for such an easy job.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.350
Cut the pretence.
A "barman" is what you are.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:01.070
Actually, as I'm here,
I've got something to show you.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:04.150
Are you remodelling a bar?

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.740
I am. But it's not going to plan at all.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:09.030
It's all in line with our marketing but...

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.490
As a barman, what do you think?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.750
I couldn't say for sure but...

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:15.660
But what?

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.210
But could it be that in fact
you detest bars, sir?

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.010
I was shocked.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.340
Out of nowhere he suddenly saw
straight through me.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.800
And with those words,

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:32.560
he reminded me
of why I came to hate bars.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.730
Back when I was a student,

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:39.020
having long wanted to go into a bar
to see what it was like,

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:44.610
I plucked up the courage and
pushed open that heavy door.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.860
That'll be 1000 yen.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.620
For some nuts? What a rip off!

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:53.620
Did someone introduce you
to our establishment?

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.620
Do I need an introduction to be here?

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:57.870
Your order, sir?

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.330
I'll have a beer.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.960
Do you not serve beer, here?

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.960
But of course we do.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:09.180
What does he expect from a poor student?

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:19.190
Very nice. It's just a beer but still...

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.280
Worried what people might think,
I made my second drink a whisky.

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.360
Just don't make it an expensive one!

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.580
That's when a sense of dread came over me.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:44.500
I felt myself go white as a sheet.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.010
What the hell was I to do?

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.220
Having seemingly noticed my consternation ...

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:52.840
Can I get you the bill?

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:57.770
I had come out with a 5000-yen note...

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.350
But...

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.900
It's true. I swear!

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:09.070
Why...? Why are you all
staring at me like that?

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.200
Damn it!

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:18.410
Sir. You can settle the bill
at a time that's convenient for you.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:29.920
Before I even knew it,
I was surprised to realise that

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:34.720
I had been telling him all about
the awful experience I'd had.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:40.560
May I offer you a drink on the house
to apologise for that experience?

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.310
Oh... okay.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.150
Is there a particular cocktail you Iike?

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:47.230
Let me see now...

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:51.030
Hang on a sec. Let's test out his skills.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.530
The Glass of the Gods...

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.740
I'll have your speciality in that case.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.910
Very well. In that case...

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.590
Now then, just what cocktail will
this barman concoct...

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.670
A bog-standard flavour
you can find anywhere?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.880
Or maybe an improperly poured
pousse-café style?

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:20.100
Whatever the case, as with that Martini,
he still hasn't checked if I ate or not...

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:24.140
Let's see what "Glass of the Gods"
this man conjures up.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:27.480
Well? Well? Well...?

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.990
First, a short quiz if I may...

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:43.080
There are two professions in this world
where the customers must not be deceived.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:48.000
The first is pharmacists and physicians,
and what do you think the second is?

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:52.300
Bartenders.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:01.970
What is he making me?

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:05.480
He's even breaking that Eden hall
sculpture he's supposed to protect.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.360
What on earth is he doing?

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:11.400
The answer is simple.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:15.900
Why is it that physicians and bartenders
must not deceive customers?

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.700
Because, with only a small change
to the recipe,

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:22.540
both have the power to create
either a poison or a medicine.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.420
A mizuwari.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:38.550
Are you kidding me?
Water mixed with whisky as an apology?

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:43.390
The mizuwari is a style of drinking
thought up by Japanese whisky companies

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.060
as a way of increasing sales!

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.890
Why even bother...?

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:54.070
I've never had a mizuwari like this...

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:58.950
Only a faint aroma from the cask, with
sweetness from the grain. And such depth.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:03.740
The edge of the alcohol is gone yet
doesn't taste watered down at all.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:08.250
The whisky is a popular blend but
it's never tasted so delicious.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:11.540
How is it possible to create
such a fantastic mizuwari?

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:15.590
This is more than a simple mix of water
and whisky, this truly is a "cocktail".

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:20.050
You must tell me, what is it that's
so different about this cocktail of yours?

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:22.600
You, sir, the weary customer.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:27.230
You have not returned home for days
because of this bar remodelling project.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.020
How did you know that?

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.940
Your shirt sleeve has stains on it.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:35.440
That seems unusual for someone
who works in hospitality.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:41.320
Your stomach is upset over the clashes of
opinion with your boss and subordinates.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.830
But you can't sleep, so you drink.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:48.460
I thought that your tongue might be tired
of getting hit with strong alcohol,

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.120
so I lowered the ratios a bit...

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:53.590
No... it's true this mizuwari is
on the weak side,

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:55.300
but the flavour is all there.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.460
It's about the ice.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.680
I use hard ice that reduces
the alcohol content a little,

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:04.390
but which doesn't melt straight away
and destroy the balance of flavours.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.600
Ice...? But...

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.640
What about the Eden hall glass that
must not be broken...?

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.900
Destroyed for the sake of
a single beverage. And...

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:19.400
for a customer who called you
a mere barman at that...

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.490
Do you know why they call us "bartenders"?

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:27.870
Why?

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.380
The "bar" is where people perch.
And "tender" means "gentle".

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:37.420
Put the two together and
you have a "gentle perch".

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.340
This wooden counter is the bar.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:44.340
On its own, it is no more
than a liquor counter.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.140
But with the bartender there,

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:50.520
the genteel nature of the bar
is brought to life.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.560
So, that is a bartender...?

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.650
That bartender back then...

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:07.240
He must have believed that
I'd come back and pay the bill.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.080
The Glass of the Gods.

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:16.750
For him, it probably was
that single mizuwari.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:22.050
The broken Eden hall glass.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:25.970
But the fairies are sure
to come back soon.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:35.230
Welcome.

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:41.110
That was my curious first encounter
with Eden hall.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:46.030
And thankfully, as you can see,
I completed the remodelling of my bar.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:50.410
Yes, it was that young man who taught me...

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:54.040
that without the gentle human touch,
it cannot be called a bar.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:58.960
I hope to welcome you here, soon.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:13.850
RECIPE: CREME DE CACAO 20ml CREME DE
MENTHE 20ml FRESH CREAM 20ml

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:38.100
Next time, "MENU FROM THE HEART".
